„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ7For the Son of man is come to save that which was lost.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¹How think ye? if a man have an hundred sheep, and one of them be gone astray, doth he not leave the ninety and nine, and goeth into the mountains, and seeketh that which is gone astray?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙˆAnd if so be that he find it, verily I say unto you, he rejoiceth more of that sheep, than of the ninety and nine which went not astray.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙjEven so it is not the will of your Father which is in heaven, that one of these little ones should perish.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŸMoreover if thy brother shall trespass against thee, go and tell him his fault between thee and him alone: if he shall hear thee, thou hast gained thy brother.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙBut if he will not hear thee, then take with thee one or two more, that in the mouth of two or three witnesses every word may be established.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ›And if he shall neglect to hear them, tell it unto the church: but if he neglect to hear the church, let him be unto thee as an heathen man and a publican.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ”Verily I say unto you, Whatsoever ye shall bind on earth shall be bound in heaven: and whatsoever ye shall loose on earth shall be loosed in heaven.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ£Again I say unto you, That if two of you shall agree on earth as touching any thing that they shall ask, it shall be done for them of my Father which is in heaven.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙYFor where two or three are gathered together in my name, there am I in the midst of them.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙuThen came Peter to him, and said, Lord, how oft shall my brother sin against me, and I forgive him? till seven times?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ]Jesus saith unto him, I say not unto thee, Until seven times: but, Until seventy times seven.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙiTherefore is the kingdom of heaven likened unto a certain king, which would take account of his servants.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ_And when he had begun to reckon, one was brought unto him, which owed him ten thousand talents.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙBut forasmuch as he had not to pay, his lord commanded him to be sold, and his wife, and children, and all that he had, and payment to be made.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙrThe servant therefore fell down, and worshipped him, saying, Lord, have patience with me, and I will pay thee all.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙbThen the lord of that servant was moved with compassion, and loosed him, and forgave him the debt.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse"¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙºBut the same servant went out, and found one of his fellowservants, which owed him an hundred pence: and he laid hands on him, and took him by the throat, saying, Pay me that thou owest.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙvAnd his fellowservant fell down at his feet, and besought him, saying, Have patience with me, and I will pay thee all.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙQAnd he would not: but went and cast him into prison, till he should pay the debt.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙxSo when his fellowservants saw what was done, they were very sorry, and came and told unto their lord all that was done.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‹Then his lord, after that he had called him, said unto him, O thou wicked servant, I forgave thee all that debt, because thou desiredst me:¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ]shouldest not thou also have had compassion on thy fellowservant, even as I had pity on thee?¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙjAnd his lord was wroth, and delivered him to the tormentors, till he should pay all that was due unto him.¦layout ªlast_verse"…¤book'§chapter«first_verse#ªlast_verse#¦verses‘„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙSo likewise shall my heavenly Father do also unto you, if ye from your hearts forgive not every one his brother their trespasses.¦layout ªlast_verse#